1
00:00:14,220 --> 00:00:18,420
Aiming for the sunset
floating over the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:19,180 --> 00:00:23,580
I kicked a pebble and let
it fly until it was gone.

3
00:00:24,260 --> 00:00:29,420
To the gym teacher's head,
while I was joking around,

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,800
they laughed at me for staying
just as cheerful as ever.

5
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:37,440
Even if I somehow stir up some good spirit,

6
00:00:37,440 --> 00:00:38,680
there's only one way: to win.

7
00:00:38,680 --> 00:00:41,940
One nightmare after another,
the unchanging streets

8
00:00:41,940 --> 00:00:43,880
are gentler still.

9
00:00:44,560 --> 00:00:46,860
Because the crows are cawing,

10
00:00:46,860 --> 00:00:48,700
the sun has already set.

11
00:00:49,800 --> 00:00:51,940
Yakitori, grilled skewers,

12
00:00:51,940 --> 00:00:53,840
even just seeing them...

13
00:00:54,660 --> 00:00:57,500
of the pointed cap,

14
00:00:57,500 --> 00:01:02,700
from the waterworks,
along with the huge power lines,

15
00:01:02,700 --> 00:01:04,080
the sunset falls.

16
00:01:06,700 --> 00:01:10,100
Tomorrow too,
it'll end the same way, won't it?

17
00:01:10,100 --> 00:01:12,800
Katsushika, for a while, they say, is happy.

18
00:01:12,800 --> 00:01:14,660
I only realized it after I lost it.

19
00:01:14,660 --> 00:01:16,300
Because I'm such a fool.

20
00:01:25,220 --> 00:01:26,940
Lemon's Strike

21
00:01:31,400 --> 00:01:32,120
What was that?

22
00:01:33,060 --> 00:01:35,320
Did Gewalt go to Europe?

23
00:01:35,740 --> 00:01:38,640
He wants to set up a branch in Paris and London,
apparently.

24
00:01:39,500 --> 00:01:41,900
That old lady's as lively as ever.

25
00:01:42,640 --> 00:01:43,000
What?

26
00:01:44,320 --> 00:01:45,860
It's a fake brand car, you know.

27
00:01:46,580 --> 00:01:48,020
What a terrible dealer.

28
00:01:48,020 --> 00:01:50,940
Japanese people are so into brand-name stuff,
after all.

29
00:01:51,700 --> 00:01:54,620
Yet plenty of people can't tell the
difference even after eating it, right?

30
00:01:54,620 --> 00:01:56,920
Is our rice okay, though?

31
00:01:57,320 --> 00:02:00,660
Don't worry,
the young lady is out gathering information.

32
00:02:00,660 --> 00:02:02,560
Lemon is out gathering information?

33
00:02:03,140 --> 00:02:04,460
She's doing it right now.

34
00:02:30,980 --> 00:02:31,260
Mm.

35
00:02:32,320 --> 00:02:36,500
Niigata, Uonuma's Koshihikari.

36
00:02:37,760 --> 00:02:40,980
That's 100 percent, Mom.

37
00:02:41,760 --> 00:02:44,560
Uonuma Koshihikari, 100 percent.

38
00:02:44,560 --> 00:02:49,620
Here it is, the real thing. Thank you.

39
00:02:49,620 --> 00:02:54,180
100 percent. Here's the next one.

40
00:02:59,260 --> 00:03:02,926
Sasanishiki 80%, Akita Bijin 10%,

41
00:03:02,976 --> 00:03:05,100
Echigo-nishiki 10%, that's it.

42
00:03:06,440 --> 00:03:08,325
Ha Sasanishiki 80,

43
00:03:08,375 --> 00:03:11,520
Akita Bijin 10, Echigo Nishiki 10.

44
00:03:11,520 --> 00:03:15,200
What? So it was mixed after all?

45
00:03:15,200 --> 00:03:17,440
Is mine going to be all right?

46
00:03:17,440 --> 00:03:18,860
Hurry up and investigate.

47
00:03:18,860 --> 00:03:22,560
She's really out doing the legwork.

48
00:03:22,560 --> 00:03:25,740
Rice appraisers from within Sotokanda too.

49
00:03:25,740 --> 00:03:29,040
Don't ask kindergartners
to do stuff like that.

50
00:03:29,720 --> 00:03:34,120
Phew, that's the end of it.

51
00:03:34,120 --> 00:03:35,880
Good work.

52
00:03:35,880 --> 00:03:36,460
Mm.

53
00:03:36,460 --> 00:03:38,240
Then, next up.

54
00:03:39,080 --> 00:03:41,220
The summer meal prototype is ready.

55
00:03:41,220 --> 00:03:43,200
Please taste it for us.

56
00:03:44,560 --> 00:03:45,820
There's a lot of it, somehow.

57
00:03:45,820 --> 00:03:54,900
The summer set is the star of home banquets,
so, here is today's breakfast.

58
00:03:55,700 --> 00:03:59,700
There's still more?
Geez, this is a lot of work.

59
00:04:01,600 --> 00:04:06,040
Ryotsu, could you drop off a bento at
Matoi's place on your way to the station?

60
00:04:06,040 --> 00:04:11,020
Sorry, I'm off duty today,
I'm not going to that place.

61
00:04:11,760 --> 00:04:16,780
No, I'll tell him. But in return,
you haven't finished the prep yet, have you?

62
00:04:16,780 --> 00:04:21,640
Hey, Yone is heading to Matoi's place
after picking up from kindergarten.

63
00:04:22,210 --> 00:04:29,820
Right, then please. But Miss, once you've finished eating,
there's a dinner party with the famous restaurant cooking association.

64
00:04:30,340 --> 00:04:31,040
Got it.

65
00:04:34,440 --> 00:04:36,440
Hard schedule

66
00:04:46,220 --> 00:04:48,440
Lemon-chan, you've come!

67
00:04:48,440 --> 00:04:50,320
You're as cute as ever.

68
00:04:50,860 --> 00:04:52,120
Do people often tell you that?

69
00:04:53,280 --> 00:04:54,080
Cute.

70
00:04:55,900 --> 00:04:58,920
It's almost lunchtime,
so let's eat together.

71
00:04:59,820 --> 00:05:00,340
Lemon-chan.

72
00:05:01,980 --> 00:05:03,340
Sorry, Lemon.

73
00:05:03,340 --> 00:05:04,140
Saved.

74
00:05:05,280 --> 00:05:07,360
Matoi-chan's bento is amazing, isn't it?

75
00:05:07,360 --> 00:05:08,360
Show me, show me!

76
00:05:08,940 --> 00:05:09,300
Yeah.

77
00:05:11,300 --> 00:05:13,120
Chirashi sushi that looks delicious

78
00:05:13,680 --> 00:05:14,800
Want some if you'd like?

79
00:05:16,400 --> 00:05:18,480
I'd love to, but I'm on a diet right now.

80
00:05:19,660 --> 00:05:20,780
What about you, Komachi-senpai?

81
00:05:21,320 --> 00:05:23,160
I'm on one too, sorry.

82
00:05:23,800 --> 00:05:25,440
We really do need to diet, don't we.

83
00:05:25,440 --> 00:05:27,120
Dieting is important, isn't it.

84
00:05:27,540 --> 00:05:29,880
Matoi, what's a diet?

85
00:05:30,780 --> 00:05:32,500
It's getting thin and looking pretty.

86
00:05:32,500 --> 00:05:35,240
So you want to get that skinny?

87
00:05:35,840 --> 00:05:39,240
I hear men these days prefer girls who are thin,
you know.

88
00:05:39,240 --> 00:05:41,740
That's why I only eat this much for lunch.

89
00:05:41,740 --> 00:05:42,980
Me too, just this much.

90
00:05:43,900 --> 00:05:45,280
It's so tiny!

91
00:05:51,380 --> 00:05:53,880
Matoi, Mikan-chan's out!

92
00:05:54,720 --> 00:05:55,580
Coming!

93
00:05:58,280 --> 00:05:59,660
It felt so good.

94
00:05:59,660 --> 00:06:01,100
Thanks for your hard work.

95
00:06:01,100 --> 00:06:03,340
You're all warm and rosy, Mikan.

96
00:06:03,880 --> 00:06:05,460
You really warmed up well, didn't you.

97
00:06:05,460 --> 00:06:06,240
Good job!

98
00:06:20,080 --> 00:06:22,740
Matoi, you're really good at swapping things out,
aren't you?

99
00:06:23,220 --> 00:06:23,860
Hehehe.

100
00:06:23,860 --> 00:06:24,960
I'm pretty used to it, right?

101
00:06:24,960 --> 00:06:27,220
Because I was swapping out Lemon's, too.

102
00:06:34,700 --> 00:06:35,700
Lemon...

103
00:06:35,700 --> 00:06:37,220
Is something wrong, Lemon?

104
00:06:40,660 --> 00:06:42,220
No, it's nothing.

105
00:06:42,660 --> 00:06:43,520
Good night.

106
00:06:50,180 --> 00:06:51,480
What happened?

107
00:06:51,980 --> 00:06:53,480
She looked really down, didn't she?

108
00:07:03,580 --> 00:07:05,280
I've stopped the taste appraisal.

109
00:07:05,840 --> 00:07:07,780
You can't just spring that on me like this.

110
00:07:07,780 --> 00:07:09,140
Miss, please.

111
00:07:10,980 --> 00:07:13,720
I don't want to eat anything.
I've had enough.

112
00:07:14,320 --> 00:07:14,780
What?

113
00:07:16,620 --> 00:07:19,260
What are we going to do
about today's seasoning?

114
00:07:20,240 --> 00:07:21,660
Who's going to check it?

115
00:07:21,660 --> 00:07:23,000
Calm down. Thanks.

116
00:07:25,120 --> 00:07:27,440
Head Chef. I see.

117
00:07:27,440 --> 00:07:29,240
How about it, Head Chef?

118
00:07:29,240 --> 00:07:32,060
I think it's something like this, isn't it?

119
00:07:32,060 --> 00:07:32,940
Probably.

120
00:07:33,560 --> 00:07:35,900
Head chef, please have confidence.

121
00:07:37,260 --> 00:07:38,360
Is it really going to be all right?

122
00:07:39,220 --> 00:07:41,840
Anyway, everyone,
go out and gather information!

123
00:07:41,840 --> 00:07:42,400
Yes.

124
00:07:42,400 --> 00:07:45,040
Well?

125
00:07:45,580 --> 00:07:46,540
I don't know.

126
00:07:46,540 --> 00:07:48,400
It's difficult.

127
00:07:48,400 --> 00:07:51,680
We can't serve anything strange, you know.

128
00:07:51,680 --> 00:07:52,340
Yes.

129
00:07:53,500 --> 00:07:55,680
Only Lemon-chan could manage it, I'm afraid.

130
00:08:00,040 --> 00:08:02,700
It's before today's banquet.

131
00:08:05,400 --> 00:08:06,740
Would you be able to eat it?

132
00:08:09,420 --> 00:08:10,580
That's not right, is it.

133
00:08:11,720 --> 00:08:14,280
It doesn't taste like the Chōkanda style.

134
00:08:14,280 --> 00:08:17,500
Head Chef, did something happen at Chōkanda?

135
00:08:17,500 --> 00:08:19,120
No, nothing in particular.

136
00:08:19,520 --> 00:08:21,960
Excuse me, I'll go screen it.

137
00:08:23,660 --> 00:08:24,300
What is this?

138
00:08:24,640 --> 00:08:25,780
How disappointing.

139
00:08:26,860 --> 00:08:28,180
I'm terribly sorry.

140
00:08:28,640 --> 00:08:31,300
Sorry, sir, please wait a moment.

141
00:08:31,300 --> 00:08:34,220
Sorry, the rice today
just isn't quite right.

142
00:08:34,820 --> 00:08:36,380
It wasn't our usual rice.

143
00:08:36,940 --> 00:08:39,880
Lemon-chan's information-gathering
skills are amazing

144
00:08:40,520 --> 00:08:41,120
Sorry.

145
00:08:42,400 --> 00:08:43,260
Crap.

146
00:08:44,240 --> 00:08:44,860
Matoi!

147
00:08:46,500 --> 00:08:49,500
Where's Lemon? The store's in a panic.

148
00:08:50,340 --> 00:08:53,620
Don't tell me you're only now
realizing how important Lemon is.

149
00:08:54,200 --> 00:08:56,760
Matoi, did something happen to Lemon?

150
00:08:57,960 --> 00:08:59,300
Even if you ask me that...

151
00:09:00,700 --> 00:09:01,600
That's it.

152
00:09:02,360 --> 00:09:04,280
So you have something in mind?

153
00:09:04,820 --> 00:09:08,400
Maybe she's worried about
gaining weight and went on a diet.

154
00:09:08,400 --> 00:09:09,660
A diet?

155
00:09:09,660 --> 00:09:12,840
After hearing Komachi-senpai and
the others talking about dieting.

156
00:09:12,840 --> 00:09:14,940
No way, she's a kindergartener!

157
00:09:15,500 --> 00:09:18,520
But Lemon hasn't eaten much since the other day,
has she?

158
00:09:19,520 --> 00:09:20,680
Now that you mention it...

159
00:09:22,400 --> 00:09:23,280
Itadakimasu.

160
00:09:25,140 --> 00:09:26,580
Thanks for the meal.

161
00:09:26,580 --> 00:09:28,000
Are you done already?

162
00:09:28,260 --> 00:09:29,840
Then I'll take this one too.

163
00:09:29,840 --> 00:09:31,800
Come to think of it,
she really wasn't eating.

164
00:09:31,800 --> 00:09:35,460
But she's not the type to go on a diet.

165
00:09:35,460 --> 00:09:37,820
Right, I'll get it out of her directly.

166
00:09:38,800 --> 00:09:40,253
So, so, so -

167
00:09:40,303 --> 00:09:43,060
What are you talking about, anyway?

168
00:09:43,620 --> 00:09:48,020
You're not just skipping the tastings, you're not
eating your breakfast or dinner properly either, are you?

169
00:09:49,500 --> 00:09:51,160
What are you talking about, anyway?

170
00:09:52,060 --> 00:09:54,420
Are you on a diet, Lemon?

171
00:09:54,900 --> 00:09:56,420
I'm not doing anything like that.

172
00:09:56,800 --> 00:09:58,300
Look me in the eye and answer!

173
00:09:58,580 --> 00:10:00,100
I'm full, that's all!

174
00:10:02,520 --> 00:10:04,100
Your stomach's growling!

175
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:06,700
Be honest, Lemon!

176
00:10:11,000 --> 00:10:13,800
My weight has gone up to 15 kilos!

177
00:10:14,200 --> 00:10:17,520
At the spring measurement at kindergarten,
it was 13 kilos!

178
00:10:19,740 --> 00:10:20,720
That's hardly anything.

179
00:10:20,720 --> 00:10:22,060
Geez, what can you do.

180
00:10:22,060 --> 00:10:24,320
It can't be from the tasting, surely.

181
00:10:24,960 --> 00:10:26,120
That's not true.

182
00:10:26,620 --> 00:10:29,460
Day after day,
it's always just the start of a diet.

183
00:10:29,460 --> 00:10:31,120
That's what made me gain weight.

184
00:10:32,280 --> 00:10:33,820
It's only two kilos.

185
00:10:33,820 --> 00:10:36,060
You'll gain about 10 kilos in a year!

186
00:10:36,740 --> 00:10:38,560
If you keep gaining at this pace,

187
00:10:38,560 --> 00:10:40,360
in five years you'll be 65 kilos.

188
00:10:40,360 --> 00:10:42,460
In ten years, 115 kilos.

189
00:10:42,940 --> 00:10:46,140
At 20, fifteen years from now,
you'll be 165 kilos!

190
00:10:46,140 --> 00:10:49,780
By the time you're an adult,
you'll have turned into a sumo wrestler.

191
00:10:51,020 --> 00:10:52,500
No way, no way!

192
00:10:52,500 --> 00:10:57,060
You only talk about your weight, but you
haven't accounted for growing taller at all!

193
00:10:57,460 --> 00:10:58,200
That's right.

194
00:10:58,200 --> 00:11:00,820
But 165 kilos is still too much, right?

195
00:11:00,820 --> 00:11:02,460
I'm leaving now.

196
00:11:02,460 --> 00:11:03,880
Daaai, Lemon!

197
00:11:06,240 --> 00:11:07,360
Lemon-sama

198
00:11:08,040 --> 00:11:13,500
Everyone... I'm sorry.
This is all for my diet.

199
00:11:16,660 --> 00:11:17,740
Lemon-sama

200
00:11:18,260 --> 00:11:19,720
It's hopeless.

201
00:11:19,720 --> 00:11:23,060
This is bad.
At this rate, Chōkanda Sushi will go under

202
00:11:23,060 --> 00:11:25,800
and my part-time job will be gone!

203
00:11:26,380 --> 00:11:28,440
Hey, don't panic!

204
00:11:29,780 --> 00:11:32,020
As for the seasoning at Chōkanda Sushi,

205
00:11:32,720 --> 00:11:35,220
Kankichi Ryotsu has taken charge of it!

206
00:11:35,220 --> 00:11:37,160
Aaaaaah!

207
00:11:42,840 --> 00:11:49,580
How did he make Chōkanda Sushi's flavor his own so fast?
Terrifying man.

208
00:11:51,420 --> 00:11:53,960
Listen, cooking is...

209
00:11:54,300 --> 00:11:57,040
Just throw in dashi, dashi, and more dashi!

210
00:12:01,240 --> 00:12:03,780
This isn't enough! Bring more!

211
00:12:06,480 --> 00:12:07,100
Alright!

212
00:12:08,300 --> 00:12:09,660
How is it, Ryo-san?

213
00:12:10,020 --> 00:12:11,500
No good. Something's missing.

214
00:12:12,320 --> 00:12:13,600
Right, pass me the sauce.

215
00:12:13,600 --> 00:12:14,200
Pour it on.

216
00:12:15,040 --> 00:12:16,680
Sauce on dashi soup?

217
00:12:17,280 --> 00:12:20,260
In the old downtown,
it's fine to put sauce on anything!

218
00:12:24,500 --> 00:12:28,340
W-at a glance,
this isn't Chōkanda's style at all.

219
00:12:28,340 --> 00:12:30,760
I changed the seasoning a little.

220
00:12:41,180 --> 00:12:42,320
No good!

221
00:12:42,320 --> 00:12:44,060
Kankichi!

222
00:12:45,420 --> 00:12:48,280
It's over for Chōkanda Sushi...

223
00:12:48,280 --> 00:12:49,240
Yes, sir!

224
00:13:04,080 --> 00:13:06,380
At this rate, we're in serious trouble!

225
00:13:06,380 --> 00:13:08,900
Where's the young miss?

226
00:13:09,820 --> 00:13:14,520
What are you talking about? If this reaches Gepparet's ears,
all of you will be fired on the spot!

227
00:13:15,660 --> 00:13:19,760
You're right, it's our fault for relying
entirely on the young lady's palate.

228
00:13:20,180 --> 00:13:22,320
There's no point regretting it now.

229
00:13:23,960 --> 00:13:26,700
We have to stop Lemon's diet.

230
00:13:26,700 --> 00:13:28,340
But how?

231
00:13:28,880 --> 00:13:29,840
Once more.

232
00:13:29,840 --> 00:13:32,660
Leave it to me once more.

233
00:13:37,920 --> 00:13:40,380
Where is this earthquake coming from?

234
00:13:43,380 --> 00:13:44,460
Ryotsu-kun

235
00:13:44,880 --> 00:13:46,640
You called me at a good time.

236
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:51,140
Actually, our company is developing
a new diet machine right now.

237
00:13:51,140 --> 00:13:52,360
Amazing, Lemon!

238
00:13:57,360 --> 00:14:00,060
Getting fat in the first place
comes from eating too many calories.

239
00:14:00,660 --> 00:14:02,600
The best way to lose weight is exercise.

240
00:14:02,600 --> 00:14:04,140
Let's start with this.

241
00:14:06,660 --> 00:14:07,840
W-what is this?

242
00:14:08,660 --> 00:14:11,560
Can't you see? It's a treadmill.

243
00:14:11,560 --> 00:14:14,420
That's not it! Why is there a lion?

244
00:14:14,800 --> 00:14:16,780
Come on, Lemon-chan, give it a try.

245
00:14:16,780 --> 00:14:19,400
I'm scared. Kankichi, you do it instead.

246
00:14:20,500 --> 00:14:21,640
Fine, I'll do it.

247
00:14:22,380 --> 00:14:22,960
Aaaaaaah!

248
00:14:25,560 --> 00:14:29,940
First, jogging mode.
Then, life-or-death mode.

249
00:14:31,860 --> 00:14:32,800
Aaaaaaah!

250
00:14:37,020 --> 00:14:37,420
Whoa!

251
00:14:37,420 --> 00:14:38,420
Whoa!

252
00:14:38,420 --> 00:14:39,340
Whoa!

253
00:14:39,520 --> 00:14:40,220
Whoa!

254
00:14:40,220 --> 00:14:40,580
Whoa!

255
00:14:40,640 --> 00:14:41,120
Whoa!

256
00:14:41,120 --> 00:14:41,140
Whoa!

257
00:14:41,140 --> 00:14:42,960
Whoa!

258
00:14:42,960 --> 00:14:43,740
Ow

259
00:14:43,740 --> 00:14:47,620
Because I hate getting hurt like this,
I run with all my might.

260
00:14:47,620 --> 00:14:50,180
That's how the diet happens naturally.

261
00:14:50,180 --> 00:14:53,620
You idiot! How could I let Lemon
use something this dangerous?

262
00:14:53,620 --> 00:14:55,600
It seems there's still room for improvement.

263
00:14:55,600 --> 00:14:56,860
Let's try the next one.

264
00:14:59,540 --> 00:15:00,560
What is it this time?

265
00:15:00,560 --> 00:15:02,060
Can't you tell just by looking?

266
00:15:02,060 --> 00:15:03,000
Do you understand?

267
00:15:11,260 --> 00:15:14,100
If you burn subcutaneous fat like this,

268
00:15:14,100 --> 00:15:16,160
dieting is possible in an instant.

269
00:15:18,840 --> 00:15:20,800
Well then, Lemon-chan, go ahead.

270
00:15:22,220 --> 00:15:23,280
Like I'd ever do that!

271
00:15:23,680 --> 00:15:26,120
I was a fool to ask Spark for help.

272
00:15:27,180 --> 00:15:28,380
Then how about this?

273
00:15:28,920 --> 00:15:30,780
It doesn't need any explanation, does it?

274
00:15:30,780 --> 00:15:32,620
Ignore it, next plan.

275
00:15:37,920 --> 00:15:39,380
It's definitely dieting, isn't it?

276
00:15:40,620 --> 00:15:42,380
Diet, diet!

277
00:15:42,380 --> 00:15:42,960
This is...

278
00:15:48,820 --> 00:15:50,380
You're the best, senpai!

279
00:15:50,380 --> 00:15:52,940
This spiny lobster is really the best,
isn't it?

280
00:15:52,940 --> 00:15:56,200
Toromo is even more delicious when it's seared and eaten,
isn't it?

281
00:15:56,200 --> 00:15:59,940
Of course! We're grilling super
Kanpalas ingredients, right?

282
00:16:01,060 --> 00:16:03,520
Hey, Lemon, how about joining us?

283
00:16:03,520 --> 00:16:04,700
Come on over!

284
00:16:07,560 --> 00:16:10,480
Forget about dieting and eat with us!

285
00:16:11,220 --> 00:16:11,980
Come here.

286
00:16:14,260 --> 00:16:17,040
Lucky! So you're giving up on dieting, then!

287
00:16:17,660 --> 00:16:20,620
What were you saying?

288
00:16:21,080 --> 00:16:24,020
The smoke's stinging my eyes,
so I just came to warn you.

289
00:16:24,780 --> 00:16:25,760
You're persistent, aren't you.

290
00:16:25,760 --> 00:16:29,040
Alright, next up is the marbled beef steak.

291
00:16:30,200 --> 00:16:31,560
How about it, Lemon?

292
00:16:31,560 --> 00:16:34,540
I've never eaten such a thick steak before.

293
00:16:35,180 --> 00:16:36,800
The fat level is perfect, isn't it?

294
00:16:36,800 --> 00:16:39,180
It's a deliciousness I've
never tasted before either!

295
00:16:43,460 --> 00:16:45,840
What was it again? You said "Ama no..."

296
00:16:45,840 --> 00:16:47,540
Amano Iwato, you mean.

297
00:16:47,540 --> 00:16:48,600
The one with Lemon.

298
00:16:48,600 --> 00:16:49,660
Didn't work

299
00:16:49,660 --> 00:16:51,680
Kankichi, what are we gonna do?

300
00:16:51,680 --> 00:16:53,280
We still have a plan.

301
00:16:53,640 --> 00:16:54,360
Nakagawa.

302
00:16:54,360 --> 00:16:55,020
Yes?

303
00:16:55,020 --> 00:16:59,180
There was a period drama on TV
sponsored by the Nakagawa Group, right?

304
00:16:59,940 --> 00:17:01,640
You mean Tōyama no Kin-san?

305
00:17:01,940 --> 00:17:05,040
What a long day.

306
00:17:05,040 --> 00:17:05,560
Aaaaaah!

307
00:17:05,560 --> 00:17:07,700
Aaaaaah!

308
00:17:10,060 --> 00:17:13,940
Why is that Shikayama politician so thin?

309
00:17:13,940 --> 00:17:17,580
I ordered that diet thing
that's all the rage now.

310
00:17:17,580 --> 00:17:21,340
If you've got a complaint,
take it up with this Sakura Ubuki.

311
00:17:21,340 --> 00:17:25,240
Hey, does anyone get how
uncool dieting really is?

312
00:17:25,240 --> 00:17:26,060
It already hurts.

313
00:17:26,060 --> 00:17:27,880
Don't make fun of the politician.

314
00:17:27,880 --> 00:17:30,280
Come on, Ryo-san, that's not good.

315
00:17:30,280 --> 00:17:31,640
What are we going to do?

316
00:17:35,360 --> 00:17:38,800
At this rate,
the shop will go under before Mom gets back!

317
00:17:39,320 --> 00:17:41,620
Kankichi, isn't there any other way?

318
00:17:42,660 --> 00:17:44,260
No, there isn't, yes.

319
00:17:46,160 --> 00:17:47,240
Welcome!

320
00:17:47,620 --> 00:17:47,980
Yo.

321
00:17:49,120 --> 00:17:50,980
Kankichi's grandpa!

322
00:17:51,540 --> 00:17:54,420
So if you're Yo-san's grandfather,
then you're Uncle.

323
00:17:54,900 --> 00:17:56,060
Nice to meet you.

324
00:17:56,440 --> 00:17:58,060
Let's skip the formal greetings.

325
00:17:58,060 --> 00:18:00,040
What the hell are you doing here?

326
00:18:00,420 --> 00:18:03,980
I heard Kankichi was working here part-time,
so I came to see.

327
00:18:05,560 --> 00:18:06,920
Well, come on in!

328
00:18:07,740 --> 00:18:15,260
Pardon the intrusion. We're his father and mother, and thank you for looking after our son.
Not at all.

329
00:18:15,260 --> 00:18:20,000
Uncle, Auntie, it's been so long!
Please, sit down. You two, sit, sit.

330
00:18:20,560 --> 00:18:25,840
Kankichi, hot towels and tea, please. What
would you like to drink? Do you have any money?

331
00:18:26,240 --> 00:18:32,120
Tea alone would be plenty, but for now, beer.
Now, what shall we have him make for us?

332
00:18:33,320 --> 00:18:35,840
Nami nigiri is fine for me, thank you.

333
00:18:35,840 --> 00:18:37,640
Why are you holding back?

334
00:18:37,640 --> 00:18:39,420
We're family, you know.

335
00:18:39,420 --> 00:18:41,120
You'll give us a discount, right?

336
00:18:41,120 --> 00:18:42,580
Thanks in advance, kid.

337
00:18:42,580 --> 00:18:44,060
Yes, of course.

338
00:18:44,620 --> 00:18:45,420
I figured it out.

339
00:18:45,420 --> 00:18:48,540
You came because you heard Gepard was out,
didn't you?

340
00:18:48,540 --> 00:18:51,780
What, is Gepard off somewhere?

341
00:18:51,780 --> 00:18:53,540
Don't play dumb, we can tell.

342
00:18:53,540 --> 00:18:55,180
It's written right on your face.

343
00:18:55,180 --> 00:18:57,320
I don't know where you heard it,

344
00:18:57,320 --> 00:18:59,660
but this old geezer really
has ears like a hawk.

345
00:18:59,660 --> 00:19:00,960
Now, now, Ryo-san.

346
00:19:02,120 --> 00:19:03,120
What would you like to eat?

347
00:19:03,420 --> 00:19:05,980
To start, we'll have fatty tuna,
sea urchin, and abalone.

348
00:19:05,980 --> 00:19:06,800
Same for me.

349
00:19:06,800 --> 00:19:08,060
Then I'll have the same.

350
00:19:08,060 --> 00:19:10,200
Did you come here to ruin the shop?

351
00:19:14,700 --> 00:19:16,700
Tonight's dinner is this, then.

352
00:19:16,700 --> 00:19:19,020
Ooh, it looks delicious.

353
00:19:19,640 --> 00:19:22,440
It's all gone in no time.

354
00:19:25,240 --> 00:19:25,920
What?

355
00:19:25,920 --> 00:19:26,140
What?

356
00:19:26,920 --> 00:19:28,160
You lot don't have any money.

357
00:19:28,840 --> 00:19:29,700
That's enough.

358
00:19:30,040 --> 00:19:30,500
What?

359
00:19:30,800 --> 00:19:35,540
Bring me the sake flasks all together.

360
00:19:36,060 --> 00:19:37,280
And hurry up with the fatty tuna.

361
00:19:37,840 --> 00:19:38,200
Yes.

362
00:19:40,380 --> 00:19:41,100
Wrong.

363
00:19:41,540 --> 00:19:42,240
Wrong.

364
00:19:44,160 --> 00:19:44,880
What?

365
00:19:45,040 --> 00:19:46,000
What's all this commotion?

366
00:19:46,320 --> 00:19:48,800
Since Ryotsu's parents
and Gramps have arrived,

367
00:19:48,980 --> 00:19:50,520
Stop it, you two.

368
00:19:52,440 --> 00:19:54,440
So they had such good octopus in stock?

369
00:19:55,000 --> 00:19:55,620
That...

370
00:19:56,980 --> 00:19:59,800
Until you stop! Don't waste food!

371
00:20:00,400 --> 00:20:01,440
L-Lemon...

372
00:20:01,440 --> 00:20:04,840
Anyone who wastes food is
neither a chef nor a customer!

373
00:20:05,260 --> 00:20:07,000
Uh, sorry.

374
00:20:07,000 --> 00:20:10,820
Getting scolded by a little kid like this,
what a joke.

375
00:20:10,820 --> 00:20:12,620
These guys are hopeless.

376
00:20:12,620 --> 00:20:15,820
Kankichi! Pops! Clean up properly!

377
00:20:15,920 --> 00:20:17,040
Yeah...

378
00:20:17,040 --> 00:20:18,060
Kankichi! Here!

379
00:20:19,140 --> 00:20:20,420
Wait up, Lemon.

380
00:20:21,100 --> 00:20:22,300
What is it, Kankichi?

381
00:20:22,300 --> 00:20:26,240
Even your skipping
breakfast and dinner to diet,

382
00:20:26,240 --> 00:20:29,140
is just as much a waste of food, you know.

383
00:20:29,140 --> 00:20:30,420
If you're going to say that,

384
00:20:31,220 --> 00:20:33,940
what, kids these days are dieting?

385
00:20:34,540 --> 00:20:37,620
At this rate,
you'll turn into an idiot like this guy.

386
00:20:37,620 --> 00:20:38,900
You're the idiot here.

387
00:20:38,900 --> 00:20:39,940
What did you say?

388
00:20:41,500 --> 00:20:42,600
Lemon

389
00:20:42,600 --> 00:20:44,780
Leave Mai and the others to me.

390
00:20:45,260 --> 00:20:49,120
Honestly, the men in this family
just don't understand how girls feel.

391
00:20:51,160 --> 00:20:52,780
What is it you want to talk about?

392
00:20:52,780 --> 00:20:55,400
This is the first time we've met,
isn't it, Lemon-chan?

393
00:20:55,400 --> 00:20:58,380
I'm Yone, Kankichi's mother.

394
00:20:59,140 --> 00:21:02,720
Lemon-chan,
won't you talk with me for a little while?

395
00:21:02,720 --> 00:21:11,480
When I was a little girl, my dream was

396
00:21:11,480 --> 00:21:14,420
to eat until my belly was full.

397
00:21:14,420 --> 00:21:16,500
You never got to eat your fill?

398
00:21:17,020 --> 00:21:17,900
That's right.

399
00:21:20,180 --> 00:21:21,940
You see, there was a war back then.

400
00:21:27,740 --> 00:21:31,100
Tokyo was burned to a flat wasteland,

401
00:21:31,620 --> 00:21:34,780
and it wasn't an era when you
could eat whatever you wanted.

402
00:21:36,140 --> 00:21:37,800
There wasn't even any rice,

403
00:21:38,680 --> 00:21:42,500
so all we could eat was sweet
potato porridge or suiton dumplings.

404
00:21:43,740 --> 00:21:46,340
Even the school grounds
were turned into fields,

405
00:21:47,900 --> 00:21:48,760
and we grew crops there.

406
00:21:49,780 --> 00:21:51,840
But we were still so hungry,

407
00:21:52,500 --> 00:21:56,100
so my classmates and I would sneak
into the fields and eat sweet potatoes.

408
00:21:56,100 --> 00:21:57,860
You ate them raw?

409
00:21:58,320 --> 00:21:58,760
Yes.

410
00:21:59,560 --> 00:22:01,660
I can never forget that taste.

411
00:22:04,280 --> 00:22:06,480
Hasn't Lemon-chan gotten fatter?

412
00:22:07,060 --> 00:22:10,140
She's growing so she can become an adult.

413
00:22:10,940 --> 00:22:11,820
Growing?

414
00:22:12,200 --> 00:22:15,940
Kids eat a lot so they can grow up fast.

415
00:22:17,900 --> 00:22:18,460
I think she has.

416
00:22:20,550 --> 00:22:21,300
Everyone!

417
00:22:31,360 --> 00:22:33,800
The young lady's going to taste-test for us again,
they say.

418
00:22:33,800 --> 00:22:34,840
Yay!

419
00:22:34,840 --> 00:22:37,760
Chōkanda Sushi's flavor is
finally going back to normal!

420
00:22:37,760 --> 00:22:39,480
We won't get fired after all!

421
00:22:41,080 --> 00:22:42,860
Lemon-chan's back again?

422
00:22:43,800 --> 00:22:44,940
Sorry, Lemon.

423
00:22:45,980 --> 00:22:47,680
I'm skipping meals today.

424
00:22:48,080 --> 00:22:50,360
I'm going on a skipping diet too.

425
00:22:50,740 --> 00:22:53,020
Neither of you should be dieting!

426
00:22:53,020 --> 00:22:55,820
You have to eat properly
while you're still growing!

427
00:22:55,820 --> 00:22:56,888
Um,

428
00:22:56,938 --> 00:23:00,740
I think we're past our
growing years, though.

429
00:23:00,740 --> 00:23:02,460
No dieting!

430
00:23:06,120 --> 00:23:07,480
Welcome!

431
00:23:10,640 --> 00:23:13,480
Mikan, eat every last bit.

432
00:23:13,480 --> 00:23:15,240
She's still growing!

433
00:23:16,940 --> 00:23:19,360
Lemon's really changed, hasn't she?

434
00:23:19,760 --> 00:23:22,440
She's acting like a nagging auntie.

435
00:23:22,440 --> 00:23:24,480
Ryo-san, about this...

436
00:23:25,940 --> 00:23:26,640
One million?

437
00:23:27,040 --> 00:23:29,420
Uncle said to put it on Ryo-san's tab.

438
00:23:29,420 --> 00:23:30,360
What?

439
00:23:30,880 --> 00:23:33,060
Hey, you're on night shift today,
can't you make it?

440
00:23:33,060 --> 00:23:34,360
I have to get to the police box.

441
00:23:35,100 --> 00:23:37,680
Damn, they took advantage of the chaos.

442
00:23:38,180 --> 00:23:41,580
Damn it, I'll make them pay no matter what!

443
00:24:01,080 --> 00:24:04,700
Sandals anytime, scandal anytime,
don't mind it, they say

444
00:24:04,700 --> 00:24:05,540
don't mind it

445
00:24:05,540 --> 00:24:08,500
Playing it cool, every day

446
00:24:08,500 --> 00:24:09,680
every day

447
00:24:10,200 --> 00:24:14,000
Boredom? I crumpled it into
a reprimand and tossed it away

448
00:24:15,080 --> 00:24:18,560
Bare instincts, raw instincts,
going totally wild

449
00:24:18,560 --> 00:24:19,460
going wild

450
00:24:19,460 --> 00:24:22,340
Reckless and broke, so what?

451
00:24:22,340 --> 00:24:23,340
Isn't that right?

452
00:24:24,260 --> 00:24:28,140
My way, however I like, that's all I'll do

453
00:24:28,140 --> 00:24:32,700
Chief Ohara's thunder, smoke from the head

454
00:24:33,580 --> 00:24:36,120
Run away and you'll rise like a tortoise

455
00:24:36,120 --> 00:24:37,440
Well, how wonderful

456
00:24:38,260 --> 00:24:41,940
In flowering Edo,
a typhoon of cool mountains

457
00:24:43,200 --> 00:24:45,400
Raging wild

458
00:24:45,400 --> 00:24:47,420
Play it hot, Cubite

459
00:24:47,420 --> 00:24:50,260
Jugame, jugame, heart, go wild

460
00:24:51,700 --> 00:24:56,440
Suigyō-matsu, Gunkō-matsu, Fūrai-matsu,
where Goo comes out is where we live.

461
00:24:57,020 --> 00:25:00,320
Yamada Construction,
Mura Construction, paipo paipo paipo...

462
00:25:00,320 --> 00:25:03,140
Shūringan, Shūringan no Gūrindai.

463
00:25:03,140 --> 00:25:06,360
Gūrindai no Ponpoko Kī no Ponpoko Nādo.

464
00:25:06,360 --> 00:25:07,940
Chōsuke, the super investigator!

465
00:25:16,280 --> 00:25:18,560
Chief, are you building a house?

466
00:25:18,560 --> 00:25:21,320
Then let me introduce
you to a good contractor.

467
00:25:21,320 --> 00:25:23,540
He's bad at business,
but his skills are good.

468
00:25:23,540 --> 00:25:24,960
I'll vouch for him.

469
00:25:24,960 --> 00:25:28,400
No, it's fine. I've got your back.

470
00:25:28,400 --> 00:25:32,060
Next time,
a Before and After makeover, okay?

471
00:25:41,160 --> 00:25:41,560
Thanks.

472
00:25:48,560 --> 00:25:49,000
Thanks for watching.

